     {
          "algorithm": "The algorithm computes a Structural Resonance Score as the harmonic mean of normalized k-core centrality and betweenness centrality, multiplies it by the natural exponential of eigenvector centrality to amplify spectral influence, and applies an exponential decay penalty modulated by local clustering and the graph's bridge ratio to penalize redundant connections, selecting the node with the highest resulting score to target high-influence core bridges while avoiding clustered neighborhoods.",
          "code": "from math import exp\n\ndef select_next_node(graph, unvisited_nodes):\n    precomp = graph.graph['precomputed']\n    max_core = precomp.get('max_core_k', 1)\n    bridge_ratio = precomp.get('bridge_ratio_high_bc', 0.0)\n    epsilon = 1e-9\n    \n    best_node = None\n    best_score = -float('inf')\n    \n    for node in unvisited_nodes:\n        n = graph.nodes[node]\n        core = n['core_number']\n        btw = n['betweenness']\n        eigen = n['eigenvector']\n        clust = n['clustering']\n        \n        norm_core = core / (max_core + epsilon)\n        \n        # Harmonic mean of normalized core and betweenness (ensures both are high)\n        if norm_core > epsilon and btw > epsilon:\n            harmonic = (2 * norm_core * btw) / (norm_core + btw)\n        else:\n            harmonic = 0.0\n        \n        # Exponential amplification of eigenvector centrality\n        spectral = exp(eigen)\n        \n        # Exponential decay penalty: higher clustering increases decay, \n        # scaled by (1 + bridge_ratio) to be stricter in graphs with many bridges\n        decay_rate = clust * (1.0 + bridge_ratio)\n        \n        score = harmonic * spectral * exp(-decay_rate)\n        \n        if score > best_score:\n            best_score = score\n            best_node = node\n            \n    return best_node",
