     {
          "algorithm": "An adaptive structural vulnerability selector that computes node scores by multiplying normalized coreness with the square root of the betweenness-to-clustering ratio and an exponentially dampened eigenvector centrality term, where the damping factor is derived from the graph's bridge ratio to automatically shift priority from bridge destruction in fragile networks to core influence in robust networks.",
          "code": "import math\n\ndef select_next_node(graph, unvisited_nodes):\n    precomputed = graph.graph['precomputed']\n    max_core = precomputed['max_core_k']\n    bridge_ratio = precomputed['bridge_ratio_high_bc']\n    epsilon = 1e-9\n    \n    # Adaptive damping: high bridge_ratio (fragile network) -> dampen eigenvector to focus on bridges\n    # low bridge_ratio (robust network) -> preserve eigenvector to focus on core influence\n    eigen_damp = math.exp(-2.0 * bridge_ratio)\n    \n    best_node = None\n    best_score = -float('inf')\n    \n    for node in unvisited_nodes:\n        n = graph.nodes[node]\n        norm_core = n['core_number'] / max_core if max_core > 0 else 0\n        btw = n['betweenness']\n        clust = n['clustering'] + epsilon\n        eigen = n['eigenvector'] + epsilon\n        \n        # Bridge vulnerability index: high betweenness, low clustering\n        bridge_vuln = math.sqrt(btw / clust)\n        \n        # Adaptive eigenvector factor: power scaling based on network fragility\n        eigen_factor = eigen ** eigen_damp\n        \n        # Composite score: core position * bridge characteristics * adaptive influence\n        score = norm_core * bridge_vuln * eigen_factor\n        \n        if score > best_score:\n            best_score = score\n            best_node = node\n            \n    return best_node",
